      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Lairich Rig",
      "description": "The Kel Burn. This photograph was taken from Sanham's Bridge; see: 987576.\nThis is a view to the west; the stream is flowing in that direction. Just one kilometre further on, it flows into the Firth of Clyde, at a point on the shoreline that faces nearby Great Cumbrae Island.\n\nThe Kel Burn gives its name to nearby Kelburn Castle.",
